          <table class="pricing-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Default</th><th>Growth<br><small style="font-weight:400;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0">10% off</small></th><th class="scale-col">Scale<br><small style="font-weight:400;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0">30% off</small></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Maps Quick</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">Up to 20 places · shares the free-call pool</small></td><td class="price-cell">$15.00<br><small>/1K</small></td><td class="price-cell">$13.50<br><small>/1K</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$10.50</strong><br><small>/1K</small></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Maps List &mdash; standard band</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;"><code>detail=0</code> &middot; up to 20 places, none enriched</small></td><td class="price-cell">$0.10<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell">$0.09<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$0.07</strong><br><small>/1K calls</small></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Maps List &mdash; premium band</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;"><code>detail=0</code> &middot; 21&ndash;100 places, none enriched &middot; flat</small></td><td class="price-cell">$0.50<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell">$0.45<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$0.35</strong><br><small>/1K calls</small></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Maps Deep &mdash; standard band</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;"><code>detail</code> 1&ndash;20 &middot; default <code>detail=20</code> &middot; up to 100 places returned, up to 20 fully enriched &middot; shares the free-call pool</small></td><td class="price-cell">$15.00<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell">$13.50<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$10.50</strong><br><small>/1K calls</small></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Maps Deep &mdash; premium band</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;"><code>detail</code> 21&ndash;100, flat &middot; up to 100 places returned, up to 100 fully enriched &middot; shares the free-call pool</small></td><td class="price-cell">$75.00<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell">$67.50<br><small>/1K calls</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$52.50</strong><br><small>/1K calls</small></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Place Details</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$1.50<br><small>/1K</small></td><td class="price-cell">$1.35<br><small>/1K</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$1.05</strong><br><small>/1K</small></td></tr>
              <tr><td class="engine-name"><strong>Reviews</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">20 reviews per page</small></td><td class="price-cell">$3.00<br><small>/1K</small></td><td class="price-cell">$2.70<br><small>/1K</small></td><td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$2.10</strong><br><small>/1K</small></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="table-notes"><div class="table-note">Maps uses the standard tier discount — 10% off at Growth, 30% off at Scale.</div><div class="table-note"><strong>Maps Deep has two flat bands, and there is a hard step between them.</strong> Every Deep call returns up to 100 ranked places by default; <code>detail</code> decides how many of those get opened and fully enriched — the rest come back as <code>core_only</code> records that still carry name, address, coordinates, rating, review count, phone and website. <code>detail</code> 1&ndash;20 is the standard band at <strong>$0.0150 per call</strong>. <code>detail=0</code> buys Maps List, from <strong>$0.0001 per call</strong> for up to 20 places and <strong>$0.0005 per call</strong> for 21&ndash;100 places. <code>detail</code> 21&ndash;100 is the premium band at <strong>$0.0750 per call</strong>, flat — 21 and 99 cost exactly the same. <strong>So <code>detail=20</code> bills $0.0150 and <code>detail=21</code> bills $0.0750: 5&times; for one more enriched place.</strong> That step is deliberate, and we would rather you read it here than find it on an invoice. The default is <code>detail=20</code>, inside the standard band.</div><div class="table-note"><strong>Read the unit before you compare us to anyone.</strong> At the default <code>detail=20</code> a Deep call is <strong>$0.15 per 1,000 places returned</strong> and <strong>$0.75 per 1,000 fully-enriched places</strong>. At the premium band's <code>detail=100</code> it is <strong>$0.75 per 1,000 places returned</strong> and <strong>$0.75 per 1,000 fully-enriched places</strong> — the same enriched-record rate at both ends of the product, which is why the premium band is fair value at its ceiling rather than a penalty. Between the two it is worse per enriched record: <code>detail=30</code> is $0.0750 a call for 30 enriched, i.e. <strong>$2.50 per 1,000 fully-enriched places</strong>. For a current synchronous call choose a depth up to 30; depth 100 requires the general job route, which is currently unavailable.</div><div class="table-note"><strong>Quick and Deep cost the same at the default.</strong> Maps Quick is $0.0150 per call and fully enriches all 20 places it returns — <strong>$0.75 per 1,000 fully-enriched places</strong>. Maps Deep at <code>detail=20</code> is also $0.0150 per call, fully enriches 20, and <em>additionally</em> returns up to 100 ranked places as <code>core_only</code> records. Deep is the better value on data per dollar; Quick is the faster, smaller response and is the one with <code>start</code> paging through the ranked list.</div><div class="table-note">Synchronous Deep requests are capped at <code>detail=30</code>. That is a <em>performance</em> limit, not a pricing one — you may ask for 21&ndash;30 synchronously and simply pay the premium $0.0750 per call. <code>detail</code> above 30, up to 100, requires <code>GET /api/maps/search/async</code> at the same flat premium $0.0750 per call, but this general job route is currently unavailable. <code>GET /api/status</code> is the authority on whether the job surface is live for your account — read <code>limits.endpoints[&hellip;].async_available</code> before you build against it.</div><div class="table-note">Search responses preserve ranked core records when detail enrichment reaches its deadline.</div></div>
      </div>

