                  <strong>eBay Full Item with Description</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">Per 1,000 direct calls with <code>include_description=1</code>. Requires funded credits. If the description cannot be delivered but the core item can, the call is charged at the standard item rate. Standard discount.</small>
                </td>
                <td class="price-cell">$1.50<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K calls</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell">$1.35<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K calls</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$1.05</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K calls</small></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-platform="x">
                <td class="engine-name">
                  <strong>X Post</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">Per 1K Requests · <code>/api/x/tweet</code> — one post by numeric id or permalink, with author, engagement counts, media, hashtags, mentions and links · Standard discount</small>
                </td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.10<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.09<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$0.07</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-platform="x">
                <td class="engine-name">
                  <strong>X Profile</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">Per 1K Requests · <code>/api/x/profile</code> — a public profile by handle, plus the recent posts it lists · <strong style="color:var(--accent);">One flat rate at every tier — no Growth or Scale discount, and we would rather print that than a discount that does not exist</strong> · <code>hydrate=true</code> adds engagement and media to those recent posts and bills 1.5&times;, so $0.15 per 1,000 calls, flat as well</small>
                </td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.10<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.10<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$0.10</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-platform="reddit">
                <td class="engine-name">
                  <strong>Reddit Search, User &amp; Community</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">Per 1K Requests · <code>/api/reddit/search</code>, <code>/api/reddit/user</code> and <code>/api/reddit/subreddit</code> — one flat charge at any depth. On search, <code>limit</code> is a page size and nothing more: one call, one charge, whether you ask for 1 result or 100 · Standard discount</small>
                </td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.12<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.108<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$0.084</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
              </tr>
              <tr data-platform="reddit">
                <td class="engine-name">
                  <strong>Reddit Posts &amp; Comments</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">Per 1K Requests · <code>/api/reddit/posts</code> and <code>/api/reddit/comments</code> — <strong>the rate buys 25 records, and every started block of 25 costs one more unit.</strong> A block is charged whole, so <code>limit=26</code> costs exactly what <code>limit=50</code> costs, and <code>limit=100</code> is four blocks: $0.48 per 1,000 calls at Default. Set <code>limit</code> on a 25 boundary · Standard discount</small>
                </td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.12<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell">$0.108<br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
                <td class="price-cell scale-col"><strong>$0.084</strong><br><small style="color:var(--text-muted);font-weight:400;">/1K Requests</small></td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="table-notes">
          <div class="table-note">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>
            Real-time data, not cached results
          </div>
          <div class="table-note">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
            Structured JSON response for easy integration
          </div>
          <div class="table-note">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>
            <strong>Three discount shapes sit in this one table, and each row says which it uses.</strong> YouTube takes the core discount &mdash; 90% off at Growth, 95% off at Scale. Nearly every other row here &mdash; Instagram, LinkedIn, TikTok, Amazon, eBay, Reddit and the X post call alike &mdash; takes the standard discount: 10% off at Growth, 30% off at Scale. The column headings quote the largest of the three, which is why they read &ldquo;up to&rdquo;. <strong>The one exception is <code>/api/x/profile</code>, which is flat:</strong> $0.10 per 1,000 on all three tiers, and $0.15 hydrated on all three. A bigger deposit does not move it, and printing the same number three times is more honest than printing a discount we do not give.
          </div>
          <div class="table-note">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg>
            <strong>Read the unit before you compare any of these rates.</strong> X and Reddit are billed <strong>per request, never per record returned</strong> &mdash; one X call is one charge whatever the profile lists, and a Reddit search, user or community call is one charge at any <code>limit</code>. <strong>The single exception is <code>/api/reddit/posts</code> and <code>/api/reddit/comments</code>, where <code>limit</code> is a price:</strong> the rate buys 25 records and each started block of 25 adds one unit, so 100 records is four blocks &mdash; $0.48 per 1,000 calls at Default, which is $0.0048 per 1,000 posts. Ask for 26 and you pay for 50. That curve is printed here rather than discovered on an invoice.
          </div>
          <div class="table-note">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5z"/><path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5"/><path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5"/></svg>
            <strong>The free calls are one shared allowance, not one per product.</strong> Every endpoint in this table draws from the same pool as Web, News, Maps and the rest &mdash; a free call is one call whatever its depth or how many field groups it asks for. A hydrated X profile spends one free call, not one and a half, and a 100-record Reddit listing spends one, not four: the free pool counts calls, never multipliers or blocks. <strong>eBay full items and paginated jobs require funded credits. The other exception is TikTok Media:</strong> adding <code>include_media</code> makes that call paid, always.
          </div>
          <div class="table-note">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
            <strong>Empty responses are refunded automatically when the search could not be completed.</strong> If we ran out of time, or could not complete the search for another reason on our side, its credits are returned to your account. <strong>A search that completes and genuinely has no matches is a delivered result and is charged</strong> &mdash; &ldquo;there is nothing here&rdquo; is a real answer to a real question. A response that is short of what you asked for is also a delivered response and is charged normally.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Rate-stability footnote (discreet, per product decision) -->
    <p style="text-align:center;font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-1rem auto 1.5rem;max-width:780px;line-height:1.5;">
      Existing credit keeps its original schedule. New deposits use the current schedule at the tier earned by the largest qualifying single deposit. Refunded or charged-back deposits can change that qualification.
    </p>

