    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <section class="faq-section" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
      <h2>Frequently Asked <span class="accent">Questions</span></h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">Everything you need to know about our pricing</p>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          How does billing work?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Serpent API uses a pay-as-you-go credit system. Deposit funds into your account and credits are deducted per API call based on the engine and endpoint used. No subscriptions or recurring charges. Your deposited credits never expire (promotional bonus credits expire 30 days after they're granted — see below).
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          What's the minimum deposit?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            For new users, the minimum to get started is $10. Once your lifetime deposits reach $50, the minimum for any further top-up is $100 — so established accounts add credits in larger blocks. New Web credit uses $0.30/1K on Growth after one $100 deposit, $0.10/1K on Scale after one $500 deposit, or $0.03/1K on Enterprise after one $1,000 deposit, so the larger minimum lines up with the tier thresholds. Refunded or charged-back amounts don't count toward your tier.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          How do pricing tiers work?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            A single qualifying $100 deposit earns Growth pricing for new credit, $500 earns Scale, and $1,000 earns Enterprise. Existing credit keeps its old price schedule. Refunded or charged-back amounts do not count toward qualification. Concurrency, minute/hour limits and queue priority follow live spendable balance, independently of the price schedule. Daily allowance is at least 10,000 requests/day for every account, including free accounts, or 100,000/day after verified total net deposits of $500; higher balance bands keep their higher daily limits. Goodwill and bonus credit do not count; refunds and chargebacks reduce qualifying deposits. Reviewed custom daily allocations take precedence. Bonus credit adds spendable balance but does not count as a qualifying deposit.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          What payment methods do you accept?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            We accept all major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express) through our secure payment partner Dodo Payments. All transactions are SSL encrypted and processed securely.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          Do credits expire?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Your <strong>deposited credits never expire</strong> — once added, they stay in your account until used, with no monthly fees or maintenance charges. <strong>Promotional bonus credits</strong> (for example the extra credits from a coupon match or bonus offer) <strong>expire 30 days after they're granted</strong>. Only that bonus portion expires — your deposited balance always remains. When you make API calls, spending draws from your bonus credits first, so they're used before they lapse. Your billing dashboard shows your deposit and bonus balances separately, along with the bonus expiry date.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          What happens if a search fails?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Every response we could not complete is refunded automatically to your account. One exception: a 404 for a resource that genuinely does not exist is an answer, and that call is charged.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          Can I get a refund?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Because credits are delivered instantly, purchases are generally non-refundable. We make exceptions for technical failures, duplicate charges, unauthorized transactions, or service discontinuation. Separately, requests we could not complete are refunded automatically; a 404 for a resource that does not exist is an answer and is charged. Submit refund requests within 7 days of purchase via <a href="mailto:info@apiserpent.com" style="color: var(--accent);">info@apiserpent.com</a>. See the <a href="/refund" style="color: var(--accent);">full Refund Policy</a>.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFaq(this)" aria-expanded="false">
          What does Enterprise include?
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <div class="faq-answer-inner">
            Enterprise is the published $1,000 single-deposit tier: $0.03 per 1,000 Web units on new credit, with Scale rates on non-Web categories. Standard Enterprise concurrency and minute/hour limits apply when spendable balance reaches $1,000. Daily allowance is at least 10,000 requests/day for every account, including free accounts, or 100,000/day after verified total net deposits of $500; higher balance bands keep their higher daily limits. Goodwill and bonus credit do not count; refunds and chargebacks reduce qualifying deposits. Reviewed custom daily allocations take precedence. Negotiated pricing and custom limits are available separately; contact us at <a href="mailto:info@apiserpent.com?subject=Custom%20Terms%20Inquiry" style="color: var(--accent);">info@apiserpent.com</a>.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA Section -->
    <section class="cta-section" aria-label="Call to action">
      <h2>Ready to <span class="accent">Get Started</span>?</h2>
      <p>Start with free calls on eligible endpoints today.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/login" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Sign Up Free</a>
        <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">View Documentation</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

